Agreed, though it's often worth sacrificing some long-term
optimization for short-term gains--surviving the early game is a lot
trickier than not dying in the late game.

Certainly getting to expert in a melee weapon isn't very useful for an
XL14 player, but even the to-hit bonus (and especially the damage
bonus) might be worth it for some fragile early game characters.  I'll
normally avoid it, but I've been known to break that rule in some
games. Generally, I'd  much rather advance a decent missile weapon
early on if possible.


